WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:12.360
In this sprouts teaching technique, we introduce&nbsp;
cold call; a simple question method teachers can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:17.400
use to increase attention, boost energy and&nbsp;
get a better understanding of their students.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:24.630
Teachers often raise a question and pick the&nbsp;
first hand that goes up, likely that's a good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:29.760
and motivated student sitting in the first row&nbsp;
already knowing the answer. The student who is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:35.550
less eager and less likely to know the answer&nbsp;
is dozing off in the back and that's a problem.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:41.310
With cold calls the teacher randomly&nbsp;
names a student to give the answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:44.940
J name some ideal conditions for growing rice.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:52.140
The benefit for the students is that everybody&nbsp;
gets a shot and since no student would know who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:56.790
is next they all have to pay attention&nbsp;
this gives shy students more voice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:02.640
increases the energy level and creates a feeling&nbsp;
of fellowship as all students are equally treated.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:11.070
The teachers also benefit. First, it's more fun&nbsp;
because everybody feels more engaged. Second,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.970
it's fast as he or she doesn't need&nbsp;
to wait for hands to go up. Third,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:20.190
the teacher gets a better understanding of who&nbsp;
already mastered a concept or who needs more help.

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:27.270
When you introduce cold calls we recommend&nbsp;
using simple questions to get students on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:32.940
board. Once they are prepared the level can&nbsp;
raise. In a more advanced form, teachers can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:38.010
use cold calls to moderate a discussion.&nbsp;
If Jay got the answer only half right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:43.530
the teacher could go on and say Sonia give Jay&nbsp;
a hint about the weather rice seeds seemed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:48.420
like. Then the teacher turns back to J to give&nbsp;
him another shot to get it completely right.

